* sg13g2-pll :: sim/sg13cmos5l-loop-filter-momcap (issue #23, Part of #16)
* Single-device AC extraction: one cap_cmomi instance (w/l set per instance
* below, matching ../netlist-snapshots/loop_filter.spice) plus a MOM-model-
* uncertainty band applied as a parallel ideal linear capacitor.
*
* Why a parallel ideal cap represents the uncertainty band: cap_cmomi.lib's
* own header states its density coefficients are TRANSFERRED from SG13G2's
* characterisation, not measured on SG13CMOS5L silicon, and cornerCAP.lib's
* own header confirms every corner/mismatch/stat section maps to the SAME
* nominal model (no characterised spread at all) -- so there is no PDK knob
* to sweep for this uncertainty. A parallel delta capacitor of value
* +/-MOM_FRAC * C_nominal is the direct, minimally-invasive way to bound
* "what if the real silicon capacitance differs from this nominal model by
* MOM_FRAC" without hacking the compiled OSDI model itself. MOM_FRAC is
* applied uniformly (same sign, same magnitude) to every cap_cmomi instance
* in a given corner run, representing a *systematic* model/coefficient bias
* (the kind of error a wrong density-transfer coefficient would cause) --
* not independent per-instance mismatch, which cap_cmomi's own model
* explicitly does not characterise either (see the .lib header above) and is
* a materially different, still-open risk this record does not attempt to
* bound.
*
* Template placeholders (substituted by ../testbench/run.sh, not meant to be
* run directly): @W@, @L@ (device geometry), @MOM_FRAC@ (uncertainty
* fraction, e.g. 0.20 or -0.20), @TEMP@ (degC).

.include $PDK_ROOT/$PDK/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cap_cmomi.lib
.option scale=1 temp=@TEMP@

Xcap n1 0 cap_cmomi w=@W@ l=@L@ mmin=1 mmax=4 feed=double subblock=0 m=1 mm_ok=1
Rbleed n1 0 1e14
Iac n1 0 dc 0 ac 1

.control
* First pass: measure the nominal cap_cmomi value at 10kHz (flat capacitive
* region -- see ../records/RECORD-001 for the frequency-flatness check).
ac dec 5 1k 100k
let cnom = abs(1/(2*3.14159265*frequency*imag(v(n1))))
print cnom
.endc
.end
